WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.770
- Drunk on a horse is
not only a great idea

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:03.833
for a country song, but it's also a crime.

00:00:03.833 --> 00:00:08.833
♪ It ain't drunk driving
if you're riding a horse ♪

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.430
- Now, the police in
Whittier, California arrested

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:13.860
a person on suspicion of
driving under the influence

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.080
after riding a horse through traffic.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.460
Police said that the horseback rider

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:18.990
was galloping through traffic

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:20.820
and refused to pull the horse over.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.680
This led to a brief chase, which ended

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.320
when the allegedly inebriated
rider simply gave up.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.750
California law prohibits drunk riding.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:30.840
California Vehicle Code
Section 21050 states

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.060
that people riding an
animal on state roadways

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:35.220
are subject to all of
the duties applicable

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:36.330
to the driver of a vehicle,

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.250
except those provision
which by their very nature

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.630
can have no application.

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:41.430
That means you can't drink and ride

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:45.120
if you are above the legal
blood alcohol limit of 0.08%.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.190
So if this is the anonymous
rider's first DUI,

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:48.720
they face imprisonment of up to six months

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:50.850
and a maximum fine of $1,000.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.590
And when a reporter asked,
"Why the long face?"

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:53.940
He replied, "I'm a horse,

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:56.590
and my rider just got pulled
over for drunk driving."

